<title>UK: Peptide Therapeutics starts Phase I trial.</title>
<headline>Peptide Therapeutics starts Phase I trial.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Peptide Therapeutics Group Plc said on Monday it began a Phase I clinical trial of its peptide product for the treatment of allergies.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, the company said drugs giant SmithKline Beecham Plc bought an option to license the peptide, which can be administered by intranasal spray.</p>
<p>The trial at Central Middlesex Hospital in London will include 36 pollen-sensitive volunteers and be conducted to establish clinical tolerance and safety.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
